International Chronostratigraphic Chart — ICS and IUGS (@geo-chart: 0, is #reference, #part-of @geo-sources) { r_6RWJCRCKJD7BZS5RRKVKGE8MT3
International Commission on Stratigraphy/IUGS. International Chronostratigraphic Chart. [Official chart](https://stratigraphy.org/chart/) · [Static editions, translations, and update notes](https://stratigraphy.org/supplementary) · [English 2026/06 PDF](https://stratigraphy.org/ICSchart/ChronostratChart2026-06.pdf).

Read the legend, hierarchy, boundaries, uncertainty/definition notes, and edition information before interpreting geological ages. Compare time units with the corresponding rock units and the defining evidence. The current static English page identifies 2026/06; the same supplementary page lists Brazilian Portuguese under 2024/12 and contains older dynamic-chart/update text. Preserve these edition differences rather than calling every available translation current.

Use the chart as a reference, not a substitute for stratigraphic reasoning or a claim that every boundary is measured identically. Preserve ICS and component-use notices when reusing a graphic. Official locations, available static edition, and translation dates checked on 29 October 2026. No chart/data collection is mirrored or ingested.

